      "prefLabel": "Session record",
      "title": "Session record",
      "notation": "session-record",
      "description": "A session's context — who is acting, which instances are open, what it waits on. A MECHANICAL role: written to as the session moves and read by a sibling deciding whether a claim is live, and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan`, `corpus` and `log`, the other stores. It carries `session-context` because the shape of what is written IS the discipline here — unlike `work-plan`, whose store has a CLI, this one is written by a machine that may be an LLM playing the part, so the schema is the contract.",
